-- title:
--   An Atkin–Lehner automorphism sending j to j(qᵖ)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 1$ a natural number with $p\nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $\{p\}$, so $L=\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$. Let $K_1$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ (the Laurent series field `LaurentSeries L`) which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M p)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to L$, of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the set [`ModularCurve.intFormRatiosC ℚ (Gamma1 M ⊓ Gamma0 p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L83) attached to the group $\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)$. Let $j\in K_1$ be an element whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $=q^{-1}\cdot$ (the power series `jNumQ`), the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. The conclusion is that there exists an $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $K_1$ whose value at $j$ has image in $L((q))$ the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ p ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), the Laurent series obtained from the $q$-expansion of $j$ by multiplying all exponents by $p$, i.e. $\sigma(j)=j(q^p)$.
--
--   On function fields this is the action of the Atkin–Lehner (level-$p$) involution $w_p$ of $X(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p))$, which on the Tate curve realises the quotient by $\mu_p$ and hence sends the $q$-expansion of $j$ to $j(q^p)$. It feeds the combined statement [`ModularCurve.XOneGammaZeroP.exists_algEquiv_map_j_eq_qExpand_and_chartAlgFin_iff_and_comap_ne_x1x0_gamma0`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneGammaZeroP.exists_algEquiv_map_j_eq_qExpand_and_chartAlgFin_iff_and_comap_ne_x1x0_gamma0), used in the analysis of the fibre structure and cusps of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneGammaZeroP_exists_algEquiv_map_j_eq_qExpand_x1x0_gamma0.lean

